de --test` still exits 0 on a conformant fixture (oracle/judge provably non-gating â€” PRINCIPLE-D).\n100\t- **Given** the WITHOUT-ledger ship-state, **When** v1 is assessed, **Then** the anti-laundering law runs as\n101\t  the honor-system checklist and a canary asserts B2â€²/B7â€² stamped BLOCKED-this-cycle + non-gating.\n102\t\n103\t## Wave 8 â€” Elevation-oracle harness + tooling + power-calc CODE (deterministic)\n104\t**Serves:** NS5 (the instrument; the RULING is H1/H2). **Increment 3-code â€” AUTONOMOUS project-DONE.**\n105\t**Done-when:** the `elevations.jsonl` fixture-construction TOOLING + the paired A/B harness (cross-family judge\n106\tADAPTER, position-swap-with-agreement, length-control, answer-key scorer, CAT secondary, per-pillar baselines)\n107\t+ the power-calc CODE are built with DETERMINISTIC unit tests green in `node --test`. NO feasibility verdict,\n108\tNO ICC, NO advisory ruling is in this done-when â€” those are H1/H2.\n109\t- **Given** synthetic fixtures with known answer keys, **When** the harness scorer + power-calc run in unit\n110\t  tests, **Then** they produce the expected deterministic outputs (the harness logic is correct).\n111\t- **Given** the harness is built, **When** `node --test` runs, **Then** it exits 0 (the oracle's eventual\n112\t  VERDICT remains advisory, never a gate).\n113\t\n114\t---\n115\t\n116\t## HALT-gated follow-on increments (NOT autonomous Foreman waves â€” human / external preconditions)\n117\tForeman HALTs for a human go (or an external-precondition check) before each; each records a BLOCKED/UNPROVEN\n118\tterminal if its precondition is unmet. None has a deterministic/autonomous done-when.\n119\t\n120\t- **H1 â€” GATE-0.5a feasibility + calibration + commit (G,k) [HALT-for-human, Increment 3a].** A human builds\n121\t  â‰¥k non-circular real-history fixtures, runs the human-dual-scored ICC calibration on the harness (Wave 8),\n122\t  and the paired-test power calc; emits the feasibility verdict and commits (