BORATED; unverifiable â†’ needs_verification handoff).\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Refutation discipline (the NS4 honesty spine)\n**Serves:** NS4. **Increment 1.**\n**Done-when:** the INDEPENDENT named-defeater refuter for each high-value elevation; B-honesty passes and its\nnegative FAILS; the bounded-refuter budget path is a NAMED canary; `node --test` green.\n- **Given** an elevation whose `what_would_refute_it` is a self-rated confidence word (no named concrete\n  defeater + `refutation_provenance`), **When** B-honesty runs, **Then** it FAILS / auto-downgrades.\n- **Given** independent refuters requested beyond budget R (=3, from `prereg-constants.json`), **When** the cap\n  is hit, **Then** a canary asserts the run HALTs (no silent drop); findings below the firing threshold ship\n  SPECULATIVE with the \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp.\n\n## Wave 5 â€” ANTICIPATE (Oranges-lens bounded premortem)\n**Serves:** NS3. **Increment 1.**\n**Done-when:** a bounded premortem (subject_cardinality==1; each anticipation = a populated, well-formed\n`future_state_condition` + `enabling_assumption`); B3 + B9 pass and their negatives FAIL; the advisory\ncross-path-cost flag is wired ISOLATED (never in the gate); `node --test` green.\n- **Given** an anticipate finding with a regret/counterfactual-cost field OR subject_cardinality>1, **When** B3\n  runs, **Then** it FAILS (Crucible's Oranges engine â†’ route to a Crucible commission).\n- **Given** a present-tense anticipate finding (no populated future-state + enabling assumption), **When** B9\n  runs, **Then** it FAILS.\n\n## Wave 6 â€” SCORE / LABEL / SYNTHESIS\n**Serves:** NS4, NS6. **Increment 1.**\n**Done-when:** dual-axis (value-if-true Ã— groundedness) scoring; tiered honest labels (only REFUTED drops;\nsingle-family ceiling PROMISING); honest synthesis; B1 + B6 + B8 pass and their negatives FAIL; `node --test` green.\n- **Given** any divergent/brainstorm \"ideate\"-class finding, **When** B1 runs, **Then** it FAILS (ideation is\n  Jumper's).\n- **Given** a per-finding `degraded:true` with top-level `degraded:false`, **When** B6 runs, **Then** it FAILS.\n- **Given** a leg absent from `risk_labels`, OR a risk_label whose rung exceeds its leg's envelope rung,\n  **When** B8 runs, **Then** it FAILS.\n\n## Wave 7 â€” Increment-1 integration + PRINCIPLE-D meta-isolation + journaling = GANDALF v1 SHIP\n**Serves:** NS1â€“NS4, NS6 (the committed shippable skill). **Increment 1 â€” COMMITTED SHIP MILESTONE.**\n**Done-when:** `node --test test/*.test.mjs` exits 0 with ALL Increment-1 canaries (B1,B3,B5,B6,B8,B9,\nB-honesty,B-ceiling) + their discriminating negatives + the meta-isolation test; B2â€²/B7â€² are stamped\nBLOCKED-this-cycle and a canary asserts they are non-gating; `NORTH-STAR.md` + `journal/` + `LESSONS.md`\nscaffolding present (canary set = the test suite; anti-drift sleep gate documented).\n- **Given** the LLM/cross-family judge endpoint is made UNREACHABLE, **When** the gate runs, **Then**\n  `node --test` still exits 0 on a conformant fixture (oracle/judge provably non-gating â€” PRINCIPLE-D).\n- **Given** the WITHOUT-ledger ship-state, **When** v1 is assessed, **Then** the anti-laundering law runs as\n  the honor-system checklist and a canary asserts B2â€²/B7â€² stamped BLOCKED-this-cycle + non-gating.\n\n## Wave 8 â€” Elevation-oracle harness + tooling + power-calc CODE (deterministic)\n**Serves:** NS5 (the instrument; the RULING is H1/H2). **Increment 3-code â€” AUTONOMOUS project-DONE.**\n**Done-when:** the `elevations.jsonl` fixture-construction TOOLING + the paired A/B harness (cross-family judge\nADAPTER, position-swap-with-agreement, length-control, answer-key scorer, CAT secondary, per-pillar baselines)\n+ the power-calc CODE are built with DETERMINISTIC unit tests green in `node --test`. NO feasibility verdict,\nNO ICC, NO advisory ruling is in this done-when â€” those are H1/H2.\n- **Given** synthetic fixtures with known answer keys, **When** the harness scorer + power-calc run in unit\n  tests, **Then** they produce the expected deterministic outputs (the harness logic is correct).\n- **Given** the harness is built, **When** `node --test` runs, **Then** it exits 0 (the oracle's eventual\n  VERDICT remains advisory, never a gate).\n\n---\n\n## HALT-gated follow-on increments (NOT autonomous Foreman waves â€” human / external preconditions)\nForeman HALTs for a human go (or an external-precondition check) before each; each records a BLOCKED/UNPROVEN\nterminal if its precondition is unmet. None has a deterministic/autonomous done-when.\n\n- **H1 â€” GATE-0.5a feasibility + calibration + commit (G,k) [HALT-for-human, Increment 3a].** A human builds\n  â‰¥k non-circular real-history fixtures, runs the human-dual-scored ICC calibration on the harness (Wave 8),\n  and the paired-test power calc; emits the feasibility verdict and commits (G,k) + ICC into\n  `preregistration.json`. If â‰¥k fixtures are not feasible OR ICC<0.7 â†’ record \"elevate efficacy UNPROVEN\"\n  (Gandalf v1 ships WITHOUT the NS5 efficacy claim) and H2 is not entered.\n- **H2 â€” GATE-0.5b A/B advisory verdict [HALT-for-human, Increment 3b; precondition: H1 PASSED].** Run the\n  paired bias-robust A/B per-pillar (SITUATE vs the abstraction-equipped direct-researchPrime arm; ANTICIPATE\n  vs diagnose-core+generic-premortem); emit an ADVISORY SHIP/UNPROVEN artifact (elevate_recall lower bound +\n  false-elevation guard). A non-additive result (below margin G) emits a HALT-for-human / **North-Star re-lock**\n  notice â€” NEVER an automated descope of a locked clause.\n- **H3 â€” Machine-checked anti-laundering [external precondition: the Phase-0 commission-id ledger, Increment 2].**\n  When the shared Phase-0 ledger lands, wire commission-id minting/resolution and flip B2â€²/B7â€² + the forgery\n  fixture from BLOCKED to a passing machine-checked gate (a NEW autonomous wave can then be added). Until then,\n  the WITHOUT-ledger honor-system path (Wave 7) is the committed done-state.\n","numLines":134,"startLine":1,"totalLines":134}}}
